{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-319112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${c}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-319112" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319112" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-28"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{22}$ of the entry ${b}_{22}.$\n\n${M}_{22}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $0$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{22} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =6-(-21) \\\\  & =6+21 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-319108" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Devel