ion-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-275501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-275501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-275501" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10-z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-128030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of ${m}_{31}$ in the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}-50 & g & f \\\\ f & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & g & -5\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-128030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & g & f \\\\ ∗ & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =g\\cdot {f}^{2}-f\\cdot {g}^{2} \\\\  & =g{f}^{2}-f{g}^{2} \\\\  & =gf(f-g)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-128030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-128030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-128030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "gf(f+g)"] ["math" "gf(f-g)"] ["math" "gf+5f"] ["math" "gf-3g"] ["math" "{f}^{2}+{g}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-128030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "gf(f-g)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-69739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of ${e}_{32}$ in the matrix\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}2p & p & -q \\\\ -p & {q}^{2} & 3q \\\\ q & 0 & q\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-69739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the third row and the second column:\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}2p & ∗ & -q \\\\ -p & ∗ & 3q \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}2p & -q \\\\ -p & 3q\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2p & -q \\\\ -p & 3q\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2p\\cdot 3q-(-q)\\cdot (-p) \\\\  & =6pq-pq \\\\  & =5pq\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-69739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-69739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-69739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{q}^{2}{p}^{2}"] ["math" "-6pq"] ["math" "3{q}^{2}p"] ["math" "5pq"] ["math" "{p}^{2}-3q"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-69739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5pq"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-275502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is $18$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-275502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${c}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is $18$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =18 \\\\ 6x & =30 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-275502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-275502" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-275502" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-18240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 9 & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-18240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & -5 \\\\ ∗ & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${d}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot x-11\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =x+55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+55 & =43 \\\\ x & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-18240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-18240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-18240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-12"] ["math" "x=-16"] ["math" "x=-18"] ["math" "x=-35"] ["math" "x=24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-18240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 7 \\\\ 6 & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 7 \\\\ ∗ & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319146" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $y$ in the matrix above.\n\n$y=$\n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & ∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-2 & =10 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f9a01882929c805ae8f03f880f100764bc453c1ee7d0fe363e3949f3e61664"} {"question" "q-319129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-319129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-42614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 9k-15 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998"} {"question" "q-42614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ & 1 \\\\ ∗ & -4 & ∗ \\\\ 9k-15 & ∗ & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${m}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)-(9k-15)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6-(9k-15) \\\\  & =-9k+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9k+9 & =3{k}^{2}-45 \\\\ -3k+3 & ={k}^{2}-15 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k-18 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=3$ and $k=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef0ef501505ad15b3d918fd486037e8f3ae2d9f64de5fbc1634c9290ec735998