, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/example-4439.json" "file_sha256" "52f40ccd834aaab7ac53f555879411bf4897dc5b68d572af815dc32e7284b121"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "a5112db55b664532de0130c202c6b6e919c5c44ac143c1b3e00ea18492050162"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "a5112db55b664532de0130c202c6b6e919c5c44ac143c1b3e00ea18492050162"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "7b0302819c882ad98b46d9e471117c6f55cf0debed9240f0e7ab4734d6d5219a"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "7b0302819c882ad98b46d9e471117c6f55cf0debed9240f0e7ab4734d6d5219a"}] "usage" {"q-1099" [] "e-4441" [] "e-4439" [] "e-4440" []} "basis" 760 "retractions" [[17592186059911 :question/problem "What is the minor of $d_{32}$ in the matrix\n\n$D = \\begin{bmatrix}3s & -r^{2} & 2t \\\\ -r & 0 & r \\\\ 5t & 4r & 1\\end{bmatrix}$?"] [17592186059484 :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059484 :question/worked-solution "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 2 - 5 \\cdot 7 \\\\\n&= 2 - 35 \\\\\n&=-33\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059485 :question/problem "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x + 2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059485 :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x + 2 y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet\\begin{bmatrix}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{vmatrix}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 7x \\cdot 5 - (-3y) \\cdot (-y) \\\\\n&= 35x - 3y^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059486 :question/problem "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059486 :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet\\begin{bmatrix}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{vmatrix}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= k \\cdot 2k - 3 \\cdot (-1) \\\\\n&= 2k^{2} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2k^{2} + 3 &= 5 \\\\\n2k^{2} &= 2 \\\\\nk^{2} &= 1 \\\\\nk &= ± 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186056186 17592186056187 17592186056188 17592186056189 17592186056190] "immutable_fields" [[17592186056185 :answer-field/correct] [17592186056185 :answer-field/id] [17592186056185 :answer-field/key] [17592186056185 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
